  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Mosiah",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 5,
    "summary": "The Saints become the sons and daughters of Christ through faith—They are then called by the name of Christ—King Benjamin exhorts them to be steadfast and immovable in good works. About 124 B.C.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "And now, it came to pass that when king Benjamin had thus spoken to his people, he sent among them, desiring to know of his people if they believed the words which he had spoken unto them.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 139,
            "end": 147,
            "text": "1 Ne. 11:4 (1–5)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Mosiah 5:1",
        "book": "Mosiah",
        "chapter": 5,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "And they all cried with one voice, saying: Yea, we believe all the words which thou hast spoken unto us; and also, we know of their surety and truth, because of the Spirit of the Lord Omnipotent, which has wrought a mighty change in us, or in our hearts, that we have no more disposition to do evil, but to do good continually.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 223,
            "end": 229,
            "text": "Rom. 8:2 (1–4); Alma 5:14; 13:12. TG Man, New, Spiritually Reborn."
          },
          {
            "start": 294,
            "end": 298,
            "text": "Alma 19:33."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Alma 19:33.",
            "prettyString": "Alma 19:33",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "alma",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 19,
                    "end": 19,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 33,
                        "end": 33
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Mosiah 5:2",
        "book": "Mosiah",
        "chapter": 5,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "And we, ourselves, also, through the infinite goodness of God, and the manifestations of his Spirit, have great views of that which is to come; and were it expedient, we could prophesy of all things.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 46,
            "end": 54,
            "text": "Ex. 34:6 (5–7)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Mosiah 5:3",
        "book": "Mosiah",
        "chapter": 5,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "And it is the faith which we have had on the things which our king has spoken unto us that has brought us to this great knowledge, whereby we do rejoice with such exceedingly great joy.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Mosiah 5:4",
        "book": "Mosiah",
        "chapter": 5,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "And we are willing to enter into a covenant with our God to do his will, and to be obedient to his commandments in all things that he shall command us, all the remainder of our days, that we may not bring upon ourselves a never-ending torment, as has been spoken by the angel, that we may not drink out of the cup of the wrath of God.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 35,
            "end": 43,
            "text": "2 Chr. 15:12 (12–15); Neh. 10:29; Mosiah 6:3. TG Commitment."
          },
          {
            "start": 222,
            "end": 234,
            "text": "Mosiah 3:27 (25–27)."
          },
          {
            "start": 270,
            "end": 275,
            "text": "Mosiah 3:2."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Mosiah 3:2.",
            "prettyString": "Mosiah 3:2",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "mosiah",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 3,
                    "end": 3,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 2,
                        "end": 2
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Mosiah 5:5",
        "book": "Mosiah",
        "chapter": 5,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "And now, these are the words which king Benjamin desired of them; and therefore he said unto them: Ye have spoken the words that I desired; and the covenant which ye have made is a righteous covenant.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Mosiah 5:6",
        "book": "Mosiah",
        "chapter": 5,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "And now, because of the covenant which ye have made ye shall be called the children of Christ, his sons, and his daughters; for behold, this day he hath spiritually begotten you; for ye say that your hearts are changed through faith on his name; therefore, ye are born of him and have become his sons and his daughters.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 75,
            "end": 83,
            "text": "1 Jn. 2:12; Mosiah 15:2; 27:25 (24–26); Moses 6:68 (64–68)."
          },
          {
            "start": 211,
            "end": 218,
            "text": "TG Sanctification."
          },
          {
            "start": 264,
            "end": 268,
            "text": "John 1:13 (12–13); Mosiah 15:10. TG Man, New, Spiritually Reborn."
          },
          {
            "start": 296,
            "end": 300,
            "text": "Matt. 12:49 (49–50); D&C 11:30."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Sanctification.",
            "prettyString": "TG Sanctification",
            "references": [
