        "chapter": 5,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "And I would that ye should remember also, that this is the name that I said I should give unto you that never should be blotted out, except it be through transgression; therefore, take heed that ye do not transgress, that the name be not blotted out of your hearts.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 59,
            "end": 63,
            "text": "Mosiah 1:11 (11–12). TG Jesus Christ, Taking the Name of."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Mosiah 5:11",
        "book": "Mosiah",
        "chapter": 5,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "I say unto you, I would that ye should remember to retain the name written always in your hearts, that ye are not found on the left hand of God, but that ye hear and know the voice by which ye shall be called, and also, the name by which he shall call you.",
        "footNotes": [
